            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+space"} generalized space
            which is “locally modeled” on these, in the sense explained in the chapter
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} on categories and toposes
            \. In order to do so we
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                consider
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+space"} generalized
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspaces"} superspaces
                whose collection forms a “good category” (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
                over super Cartesian space) in that lots of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
                on general superspaces (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"}> limits
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %li
              %p
                use special properties of this nice category (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"}> differential cohesion
                ) in order to characterize and construct the good, tame superspaces, such as actual
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
          %p
            The construction proceeds in direct anology to the non-super version discussed in the chapters
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} on smooth sets
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+manifolds+and+orbifolds"} on manifolds and orbifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic
            situation.
          %p
            The following simple definitions
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSet"}
            and
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothSets"}
            are key to the whole theory. They embody the perspective of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
            (
            %a{:href => "#Grothendieck65"}> Grothendieck 65
            ). See remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ASheafAsASpace"}
            below for exegesis and illustration.
          #SiteCartSp.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"}> CartSp
                )
            %p
              Write
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in\mathbb{N}
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              between them. Say that a collection of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              if this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              in that every finite non-empty intersection of the charts is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to a Cartesian space. This defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              and hence makes it a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          #SmoothSet.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"}> smooth set
                )
            %p
              We say a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
              (this Def.ets#CategoryOfSmoothSets)) is, equivalently, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SiteCartSp"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SmoothSet \;\coloneqq\; Sh(CartSp)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#Sheaf"}> this Def.
              ) of smooth set.
          #ASheafAsASpace.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"}> functorial geometry
                )
            %p
              The useful way to think of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSet"}
              in the present context is as defining a kind of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
              which is
              %em defined
              by which smooth functions from Cartesian spaces it receives (see also at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
              for more exposition of this point).
            %p
              Namely a smooth set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSet"}
              is first of all a rule
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^p \mapsto  X(\mathbb{R}^p) \in Set
            %p
              which assigns a set to each Cartesian space. We are to think of this set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\mathbb{R}^n)
              as the set of smooth functions {“
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \stackrel{}{\to} X
              ”}, only that there is no pre-defined concept of smoothness of functions into
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              between Cartesian spaces, there is to be a corresponding function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              between these sets, going in the opposite direction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_1}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n_2}
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\mapsto
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    X(\mathbb{R}^{n_1})
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{f^\ast}}
                    \\\
                    X(\mathbb{R}^{n_2})
                    }
            %p which we are to think of as being the precomposition operation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext "
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi X
                    %mtext "
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext "
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi X
                    %mtext "
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\text{"}\mathbb{R}^{n_2} \stackrel{\phi}{\to} X\text{"})
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    (\text{"}f^\ast \phi \colon \mathbb{R}^{n_1} \overset{f}{\to} \mathbb{R}^{n_2} \overset{\phi}{\to} X\text{"})
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is required to satisfy the evident conditions that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              is respected, in that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g \circ f)^\ast = g^\ast \circ f^\ast
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi id
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id^\ast = id
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              on the category of test spaces – the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"}> functor of points
              ” (
              %a{:href => "#Grothendieck65"}> Grothendieck 65
              ).
            %p
              In addition, the requirement that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              of Cartesian spaces from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SiteCartSp"}
              means that the assignment
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \mapsto X(\mathbb{R}^n)
              knows that one coordinate system
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              may be covered by other coordinate systems. Namely let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \overset{\phi_i}{\to}\}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              (each of which may be identified with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              itself, by a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext "
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mtext "
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mtext "
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi i
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mtext "
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\text{"}\mathbb{R}^n \to X\text{"})
                    \\mapsto
                    \\left\{
                    \\text{"}U_i \overset{\phi_i}{\to} \mathbb{R}^n \to X\text{"}
                    \\right\}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\mathbb{R}^n)
              to the subset of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i}{\prod} X(U_i)
              of those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuples"} tuples
              of functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \stackrel{f_i}{\to} X
              which coincide on all
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i |_{U_i \cap U_j} = f_j |_{U_i \cap U_j}
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matching+families"}> matching families
              ”).
            %p
              For example every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              defines a smooth set by the rule
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \mapsto C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n ,X)
            %p
              which says that the set of would-be smooth functions into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the actual set of smooth functions into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represents
              a sheaf on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
            %p
              This defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusion of Cartesian spaces into smooth sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    y \;\colon\; CartSp \hookrightarrow SmoothSet
            %p
              called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %p
              The same construction works for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \mapsto C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n ,X)
            %p which assigns actual sets of smooth functions.
            %p
              Notice that since Cartesian spaces (and smooth manifolds) themselves are understood as special cases of smooth sets, there now appears an actual concept of smooth functions of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \to X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSet
              of smooth sets.
            %p
              Now there might be a worry: given any smooth set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and any Cartesian space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %em two different
              concepts of what the set of smooth functions from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is: the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\mathbb{R}^n)
              of “smooth functions by fiat” (maps with quotation marks) and the actual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi SmoothSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{SmoothSet}(\mathbb{R}^n, X)
              (maps without quotation mark).
            %p
              That these two sets are in fact in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a generalized smooth space is consistent, is the statement of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi SmoothSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{SmoothSet}(\mathbb{R}^n, X)
                    \\;
                    \\simeq
                    \\;
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              says that we may remove the quotation marks:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi morphisms
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi of
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi smooth
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi spaces
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left\{
                    morphisms\;of\;smooth\;spaces\;
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \to X
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
          #GeneralizedSpaces.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"}> generalized spaces
                )
            %p
              The strategy is now to work in the nice category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSets
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
              (a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
              of more specific types of smooth spaces having extra properties which one may need in given applications. There is a long list of such subcategories of relevance, some of these we briefly discuss now:
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
