                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                  (
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#LeftAdjointFunctorPreservesEpi"}> this Prop.
                  ), but also
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserved limit
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                  (
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#AdjointsPreserveCoLimits"}> this Prop.
                  ). This implies the claim because every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %p
                  This implies, again by uniqueness of adjoints (
                  %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#UniquenessOfAdjoints"}> this Prop.
                  ) that the composite functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\longleftarrow SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  from the previous item is in fact the functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{SuperFormalSmoothSet}
                  from the
                  = succeed "-structure" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SuperFormalSmoothSet"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  and hence, finally, that there is the bottom right adjoint
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi coDisc
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Set
                        %mover
                          %mo ↪
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                        %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        coDisc \;\colon\; Set \overset{\phantom{AA}}{\hookrightarrow} SuperFormalSmoothSet
                %p as claimed.
            %p
              Finally, that every second functor is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusion (a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  left Kan extension along
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functors"} fully faithful functors
                  is itself fully faithful (
                  %a{:href => "Kan+extension#LeftKanExtensionBasicProp"}> this prop.
                  );
              %li
                %p
                  in an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
                  the leftmost adjoint is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
                  precisely if the rightmost adjoint is (
                  %a{:href => "adjoint+triple#FullyFaithful"}> this prop.
                  ).
          %p
            Proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            says that the basic operations on local model spaces, such as
          %ol
            %li
              %p forming the underlying bosonic space,
            %li
              %p forming the underlying formal bosonic space of bi-fermions,
            %li
              %p forming the underlying reduced space
          %p extend from local model spaces to the generalized spaces modeled on them, while retaining their relation to each other and to the respective inclusions, and such that yet further operations accompanying them are induced.
          %p To record what all these operations are, it is useful to compose the functors above in pairs, with one functor projecting down to the left, and the next one including back with either a left or right adjoint of the projection.
          %p
            For example given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+space"} generalized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            to it yields its underlying bi-fermionic formal smooth space, regarded as an object in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FormalSmoothSet"} FormalSmoothSet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operator"} modal operator
            (
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#ModalOperator"}> this Def.
            ), on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SuperFormalSmoothSet"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi sup
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi even
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overset{\rightrightarrows}{(-)}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\iota_{sup} \circ even
                  \\;\colon\;
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  \\overset{\phantom{AAAA}}{\longrightarrow}
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  \\,.
          %p Similarly, composing the projection which is the left Kan extension of the underlying bosonic space operation with the canonical re-embedding yields an endofunctor that has the interpretation of sending any generalized superspace to its underlying generalized bosonic space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇝
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi sup
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi sup
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overset{\rightsquigarrow}{(-)}
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\iota_{sup} \circ \Pi_{sup}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  \\longrightarrow
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            In fact, since these two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            are obtained from the two possible composites in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            whose middle functor is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            – corresponding to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
            (
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#AdjointModality"}> this Def.
            ) – it is immediate to see that:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇝
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overset{\rightsquigarrow}{(-)}
                has the structure of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comodal+operator"} comodal operator
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇉
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overset{\rightrightarrows}{(-)}
                has the structure of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operator"} modal operator
            %li
              %p
                together they form an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⇉
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⇝
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overset{\rightrightarrows}{(-)} \dashv \overset{\rightsquigarrow}{(-)}
          %p
            Moreover, by prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FormalSmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothSet
            extends to an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            which is a further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+comonad"} idempotent comonad
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rheonomy"} rheonomy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rh
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi sup
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi sup
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Rh
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Disc_{sup} \circ \Pi_{sup}
                  \\;\colon\; SuperFormalSmoothSet \longrightarrow SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            But prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            says that there are yet further adjoints, however these no longer go between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmoothSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSet
            or even just between the former and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SmoothSet
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi FormalSmoothSet
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SmoothSet \longleftarrow FormalSmoothSet \longleftarrow SuperFormalSmoothSet
          %p which first forms the bosonic underlying space, and then forms the reduced underlying space of what remains. The total result of this operation is just plain reduction, removing all infinitesimal directions, whether odd graded or even graded. Therefore, the result of composing this operation with its right adjoint canonical re-embedding yields an endofunctor which we should call
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi inf
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi inf
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Re
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\iota_{inf} \circ \Pi_{inf}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet \longrightarrow SuperFormalSmoothSet
          %p
            and think of as the operation of reduction on generalized
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+sets"} super formal smooth sets
          %p
            Notice that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            embeddings
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{i}{\hookrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {}
          %p
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizations"} localizations
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \circ i \simeq id
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflection
            (
            %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#FullyFaithfulAndInvertibleAdjoints"}> this prop.
            ).
          %p
            In our situation this first of all means that all of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            above are idempotent, as already mentioned. But next it implies that first applying a “deep” projection in the diagram in prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℜ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇝
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overset{\rightsquigarrow}{\Re(X)}
                  \\simeq
                  \\Re(X)
          %p saying that if a space is reduced, then it has no infinitesimal directions whatsoever, in particular no odd-graded ones, hence it is already bosonic.
          %p We will denote this situation by an inclusion sign
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇝
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Re \;\lt\; \overset{\rightsquigarrow}{(-)}
          %p
            to be read “reduced implies bosonic”. This is an example of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modalities"} modalities
            (
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#PreorderOnModalities"}> this Def.
            )
          %p
            We may proceed this way with all the remaining functors in prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperFormalCartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperFormalCartSp
            which are all related to each other by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            or by this inclusion relation of projection operators.
          %p
            The result is a system of 9 endofunctors, or 12 if we inclue the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top"} top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
            (
            %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#InitialAndFinalAdjointModality"}> this Example
            ):
          %table{:style => "margin:auto"}
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ʃ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Disc
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \;\coloneqq\; Disc \circ \Pi_0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♭
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Disc
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \;\coloneqq\; Disc \circ \Gamma
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{A}
