          %h2#SuperMappingSpaces Super mapping spaces
          %p
            We now discuss
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                for the theory – mapping spaces nicely exhibit the usage and the power of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
                perspective (remark
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ASheafAsASpace"}
            %li
              %p
                for applications – in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"} superfield
                is really a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
                of a mapping space, and hence the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
                of interest in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
                (in the generality of spaces of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+sections"} spaces of sections
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
          %p
            The key idea is that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            of functions between sets have the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
          #FunctionSet.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              be two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Y^X \coloneqq \{X \to Y\}
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is characterized by the fact that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in Set
              any further set, there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom( Z \times X, Y ) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} Hom(Z, Y^X)
            %p
              between functions of two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              and functions of one variable into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Y
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(-,-)
              of two variables to the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              which sends any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              to the function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto f(z,x)
          %p
            It is immediate how to generalize example
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctionSet"}
          #InternalHom.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"}> mapping space
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"}> internal hom
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              of its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is, if it exists, a functor of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-,-] \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}^{op} \times \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            %p
              such that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+sets"} hom sets
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(Z \times X, Y)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(Z, [X,Y])
            %p
              for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y,Z \in \mathcal{C}
          %p The class of examples that we are interested in is the following:
          #SheavesHomInternal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = Sh(\mathcal{S})
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              over some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              between any two sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Sh(\mathcal{C})
              exists and is given objectwise by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of sets:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X \times Y) \;\colon\; U \mapsto X(U) \times Y(U)
            %p
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in \mathcal{S}
            %p
              Moreover, an
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternalHom"}
              exists (“generalized
              = succeed "\u201D)." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Sh(\mathcal{S})
              to the sheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X,Y] \;\colon\; \mathcal{S}^{op} \longrightarrow Set
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \mapsto Hom_{Sh(\mathcal{S})}( X \times y(U), Y )
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon \mathcal{S} \hookrightarrow Sh(\mathcal{S})
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          %p
            For the
            %strong proof
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
          %p
            Notice how prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesHomInternal"}
            expresses an intuitively most obvious statement: Applied to geometric sheaf toposes such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} SmoothSet
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothSets"}
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,Y]
            is a smooth map of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times U \to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            which is smoothly parameterized by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            The following shows formally that the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+homs"} internal homs
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
            does generalize the traditional concept of smooth
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
          #SmoothManifoldsMappingSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\Sigma,X)
              carries the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+manifold"} infinite dimensional
              (in general)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifold"} Fréchet manifold
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Frechet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(\Sigma,X)_{Frechet}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi FrechetMfd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon FrechetMfd \hookrightarrow SmoothSet
              of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsContainSmoothManifolds"}
              this coincides with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
              formed in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSet
              according to prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesHomInternal"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Frechet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Sigma, X] \simeq  i(Maps(\Sigma, X)_{Frechet})
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular for instance the smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
              of a smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is simply the internal hom
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^1,X]
          %p
            A
            %strong proof
            is given in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "diffeological+space#Waldorf09"} Waldorf 09, lemma A.1.7
          %p
            But in the topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothSets"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldsMappingSpace"}
          #CorepresentingTangentSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SuperFomalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{D}^1 = Spec(\mathbb{R}[\epsilon]/(\epsilon^2))
                    \\in
                    InfPoint \hookrightarrow SuperFomalSmoothSet
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+dual+numbers"} ring of dual numbers
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EvenPartOfDimTwoSuperpoint"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to \mathbb{D}^1
            %p Then for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \in SmoothMfd \hookrightarrow SuperFormalSmoothSet
            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} super formal smooth set
              (this Prop.ets#InclusionOfSmoothManifoldsIntoSmoothSets)), the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^1
              with this basepoint is the smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (again under the embedding of this Prop.ets#InclusionOfSmoothManifoldsIntoSmoothSets)):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mo *
                                  %mo →
                                  %msup
                                    %mi 𝔻
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [\mathbb{D}^1, X] &amp;\simeq&amp; T X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{[\ast \to \mathbb{D}^1,X]}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    [\ast,\X] &amp;\simeq&amp; X
                    }
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesHomInternal"}
              the rule for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+set"} smooth set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{D}^1,X]
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi SmoothSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \mapsto Hom_{SmoothSet}( \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}^1, X )
                    \\,.
            %p
              By prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomsOutOfFirstOrderInfinitesimalLine"}
              = succeed "-parameterized" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vectors"} tangent vectors
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              Moreover, looking at the proof of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomsOutOfFirstOrderInfinitesimalLine"}
              it is immediate that composing a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{D}^1 \to X
            %p
              representing some tangent vector in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the global point inclusion of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^1
              yields the point in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast \to \mathbb{D}^1 \to X
            %p
              at which this tangent vector is based. This shows that the vertical map in the above claim is indeed the projection from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              to the base manifold.
          %p
            Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingTangentSpace"}
            is a key observation that motivated the development of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes+of+laws+of+motion"}> Lawvere 97
            ).
          %p The following is the supergeometric analog of this situation:
          #MappingSpaceOddTangentBundle.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+tangent+bundle"} odd tangent bundle
                as
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperFormalSmoothSet
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}
              into
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesHomInternal"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+tangent+bundle"} odd tangent bundle
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OddTangentBundle"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi T X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Π
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mo *
                                  %mo →
                                  %msup
                                    %mi ℝ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mn 0
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}, X] &amp;\simeq&amp; \Pi T X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{[\ast \to \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1},X]}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    [\ast,\X] &amp;\simeq&amp; X
                    }
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+object"} bosonic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesHomInternal"}
              the set of plots of the smooth set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}, X]
              on this test space is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1},X](\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \=
                    Hom_{SuperFormalSmoothSet}( \mathbb{R}^{n\vert 1}, X )
                    \\,.
            %p
              But since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is bosonic (an ordinary smooth manifold), this is equivalently just
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1},X](\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \=
                    Hom_{SuperFormalSmoothSet}( \mathbb{R}^{n}, X )
                    \\simeq
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\,,
            %p
              which shows that the bosonic super smooth set underlying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1},X]
              is just
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              itself.
            %p
              But then consider probes parameterized by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⇝
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi ℝ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mn 2
                              %mo ⇉
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝔻
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    [\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1},X](\mathbb{R}^{n\vert 1})
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom( \mathbb{R}^{n\vert 2}, X )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom( \mathbb{R}^{n\vert 2}, \overset{\rightsquigarrow}{X} )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom(  \overset{\rightrightarrows}{\mathbb{R}^{n \vert 2}}, X )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom(  \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}^1 , X )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom(\mathbb{R}^n, T X)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where we used the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo ⇝
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightrightarrows \dashv \rightsquigarrow
              from prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProgressionOfIdempotentEndofunctors"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EvenPartOfDimTwoSuperpoint"}
              and finally example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CorepresentingTangentSpace"}
          %p
            Notice the curious difference between the bosonic and the odd-graded version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+tangent+bundle"} synthetic tangent bundle
            as seen by its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [[\mathbb{D}^1, X], \mathbb{R}] \;\simeq\; C^\infty(T X)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [[\mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}, X], \mathbb{R}] \simeq \Omega^\bullet(X)
          %p
            In the first case the, smooth functions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
            do not know about the linear structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            in the second case appear as the sub-space of that of all smooth functions on those which are graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials"} polynomials
            (over the algebra of smooth functions on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            More generally, this is the concept if
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfields"} superfields
            as used in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature:
          #Superfields.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfields"}> superfields
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
              (for instance a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InternalHom"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,\mathbb{R}]
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,\mathbb{C}]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+fields"}> scalar fields
              ”). We may understand the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
              of this superspace via its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
              which, via prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesHomInternal"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi q
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi q
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi even
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %msup
                                  %mi C
                                  %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi ℝ
                                %msup
                                  %mo ∧
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mi q
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                                %mo )
                              %mi even
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}
                    \&amp; \mapsto
                    Hom( X \times \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}, \mathbb{R} )
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \\simeq
                    C^\infty(X \times \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q})_{even}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \\simeq
                    \\left( C^\infty(X) \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \wedge^\bullet \langle \theta_1, \cdots, \theta_q\rangle\right)_{even}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here in the first line on the right we have the set of maps of supermanifolds of the form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q} \to \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              of the super-algebra of functions on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              odd generators
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
            %p Now an element in this tensor product is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %mo +
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %mo +
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f
                    +
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{q}{\sum}
                    g_i \theta_i
                    +
                    \\underoverset{i,j = 1}{q}{\sum}
                    f_{i j} \theta_i \theta_j
                    +
                    \\underoverset{i,j,k = 1}{q}{\sum}
                    g_{i j k} \theta_i \theta_j \theta_j
                    +
                    \\cdots
            %p
              for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi even
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{\cdots} \in C^\infty(X)_{even}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi ⋯
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi odd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{\cdots} \in C^\infty(X)_{odd}
            %p
              (Notice that here if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is of superdimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d_X,q_X)
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo &gt;
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \gt q_X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
              provides an arbitrary supply of auxiliary Grassmann coordinates
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
              of even and odd component functions multipled with Grassmann algebra elements to yield a homogeneously graded sum is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"} superfield
            %p
              In order to make sense of this, some physics textbooks (e.g.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bryce+DeWitt"} de Witt
              92) posit a single “infinite dimensional Grassmann algebra” from which to draw the elements
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Sachse08"} Sachse 08, section 5.2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
              perspective (remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ASheafAsASpace"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for each finite dimensional Grassmann algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet \langle \theta_1, \cdots, \theta_q\rangle = C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0\vert q})
                  superfields have an expansion in terms of the generators
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi θ
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
              %li
                %p
                  these expressions are
                  %em covariant
                  with respect to change of Grassmann coordinates
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi q
                          %mo →
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi q
                              %mo ′
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q} \to \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q'}
            %p
              There are of course the evident generalizations of the scalar valued superfields along the same lines. In general there is a (super-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi π
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{\pi}{\to} X
              over (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"}> super
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              called the (super)-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
              such that a field on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              of the field bundle (see also at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles+in+physics"} fiber bundles in physics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_X(E)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    [X,E] \underset{[X,X]}{\times} \{id_X\}
                    \\,,
            %p
              i.e. the super-space with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              that it makes the follwing
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} square commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi π
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Gamma_X(E) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; [X,E]
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{X,\pi}}
                    \\\
                    \\{id_X\} &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; [X,X]
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"} superfield
              with values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_X(E)
              = succeed "this" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+geometry"} functorial geometry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}
              a homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \colon X \times \mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ψ
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi π
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi pr
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; E
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\psi}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi}}
                    \\\
                    X \times \mathbb{R}^{0 \vert q}
                    \&amp;\underset{pr_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              In a typical example
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi Π
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = \Pi S
              is the odd version (according to example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OddTangentBundle"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Then an element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Π
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,\Pi S]
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 0}
                  no information;
              %li
                %p
                  over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0 \vert 1}
                  an element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \theta
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Γ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \in \Gamma_X(S)
                  an ordinary section of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
                  (hence a
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+field"} spinor field
            %p and so on.
            %p
              This may be combined: For example if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ̲
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi X
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{\mathbb{C}} \oplus_X \Pi
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
              with an odd
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo ̲
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi X
                      %mi Π
                      %mi S
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_X\left(\underline{\mathbb{C}} \oplus_X \Pi S \right)
              is over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0\vert 1}
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo +
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi θ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma = \phi + \psi \theta
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is a complex-vaued
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
              again a section of the spinor bundle.
            %p
              This way
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+fields"} bosonic fields
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+fields"} fermionic fields
              may be combined into a singe
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"} superfield
              (see also at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+multiplet"} super multiplet
          %h2#Supermanifolds Supermanifolds
          %p
            We now define and then discuss the analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            –
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract"} general abstract
            definition of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifold"}> V-manifold
            ” or “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-scheme” locally modeled on any given kind of model spaces to the special case where the local model spaces are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
            as discussed above. This general method is also discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+manifolds+and+orbifolds"} geometry of physics – manifolds and orbifolds
          %p
            Recall the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Re \dashv \Im)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  \\longrightarrow
                  SuperFormalSmoothSet
          %p
            from Prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProgressionOfIdempotentEndofunctors"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSmoothSetsSystemOfAdjunctions"}
            and prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartSpCoreflectiveInclusion"}
            we know that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
            sends a (formal)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
            to its underlying reduced ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Re(\mathbb{R}^{p\vert q}) \simeq \mathbb{R}^p
          %p and generally
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %mi 𝔻
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Re(\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}) \simeq \mathbb{D}^n
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔻
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}
            any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened superpoint
          %p
            This is enough to find what its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
            is doing:
          #ImAction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SuperFormalSmoothSet
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothSets"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} super formal smooth set
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Im X
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}
                    \\mapsto
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}
              any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened superpoint
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              By applying the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              that characterizes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ℑ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re \dashv \Im
              and using the characterization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
              we get the following sequence of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi 𝔻
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi 𝔻
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℜ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi 𝔻
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (\Im X)(\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D})
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom( \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D} , \Im X)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom(\Re(\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}), X)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom(\mathbb{R}^n, X)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    X(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %p
            Proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ImAction"}
            means that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for instance an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            (regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+set"} super formal smooth set
            via prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsContainSmoothManifolds"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im X
            is a rather exotic kind of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            does, but every
            %em infinitesimal
            curve or shape inside it is necessarily constant. A good way to think about this (which is also the precise way to think about it, if we speak in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im X
            is the result obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by
            %strong identifying all infinitesimally close points
            with each other. In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            this construction is often known as forming the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+shape"} de Rham shape
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (
            %a{:href => "#de+Rham+space#Simpson96"}> Simpson 96
            ). Here we will say
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape"} infinitesimal shape
          %p
            Another useful perspective on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℑ
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im X
            is the following:
          #DiskBundle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk+bundle"}> infinitesimal disk bundle
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SuperFormalSmoothSet
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothSets"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+disk+bundle"} infinitesimal disk bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^\infty X
              is the left vertical morphism in the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
