          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SuperFormalSmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in SuperFormalSmoothSet
              two ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              via prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsContainSmoothManifolds"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphisms"}
              precisely if it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              in the traditional sense.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              By remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormallyEtaleUnwinding"}
              the condition of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphisms"}
              on morphisms between smooth manifolds is equivalent to the traditional condition of being locally diffeo already when seen just under the internal hom out of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(\mathbb{R}[\epsilon](\epsilon^2))
            %p
              But, as the name suggests, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              of smooth manifolds is in particular also a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+homeomorphism"} local homeomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              there is actually an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              restricts to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
              on that neighbourhood. This implies that the full condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphisms"}
              holds, by an argument as in example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectioonOutOfCoproductIsFormllyEtale"}
          #ProjectioonOutOfCoproductIsFormllyEtale.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
